        "amount": 100,
        "unit": "g",
        "note": "green, rinsed"
      },
      {
        "ingredient": "salt",
        "amount": null,
        "unit": "to-taste"
      }
    ],
    "steps": [
      "Mix the ginger, turmeric, pepper, garlic, saffron water, 1 tbsp of the oil and a small pinch of salt into a paste and rub it over the chicken. Leave it for at least 30 minutes.",
      "Heat the remaining oil in a wide heavy pan or tagine base. Add the onions and a splash of water and cook gently for 10 minutes until soft and pale.",
      "Add the chicken, the tied herbs and the water. Bring to a simmer, cover and cook over low heat for 40 minutes, turning the chicken once.",
      "Add the preserved lemon rind and olives. Cook uncovered for 15 to 20 minutes until the sauce is reduced to a loose, glossy gravy and the chicken is tender.",
      "Taste for salt, remembering the lemon and olives are salty. Discard the herb bunch and serve with bread."
    ],
    "notes": "Rinse the preserved lemon and remove the pulp if you want a milder flavour.",
