    "steps": [
      "In a large pot, melt the first portion of butter and cook the lamb and onions with the spices for 10 minutes, stirring. Add the tomatoes, soaked chickpeas, herb bunches and water. Bring to a boil, then simmer for 1 hour.",
      "Add the carrots and turnips and cook for 20 minutes. Add the pumpkin and zucchini and cook 15 minutes more, until all are tender.",
      "Meanwhile, spread the couscous in a wide dish, sprinkle with 200 ml cold water and a little salt, and rub it with your fingers to separate the grains. Rest 10 minutes.",
      "Steam the couscous in a steamer set over the pot for 15 minutes, uncovered at first. Tip it back into the dish, break up lumps, sprinkle with another 100 ml water and rub in half the second portion of butter. Steam again for 15 minutes.",
      "Repeat once more with the remaining butter. If using quick-cook couscous, follow the packet and fluff with butter instead.",
      "Pile the couscous on a large dish, make a well, top with the meat and vegetables and ladle over some of the broth. Serve the rest of the broth on the side."
    ],
    "notes": "Number and type of vegetables vary by cook and season. Drained chickpeas can be added with the pumpkin if canned.",
